# hi's nano override, kept to the minimum that earns the --rcfile: the syntax
# definitions nano already ships, and nothing to taste. Your own file at
# $_HI_CONFIG_DIR/nano.rc replaces this one wholesale.
#
# One glob, not two. An `include` that expands to nothing is not fatal, but
# nano says so on the status bar ("Mistakes in '<rcfile>'") and rings the bell,
# which is a poor way to open a file on a fresh target. /usr/share/nano ships
# with the nano package itself; /usr/share/nano/extra is a Debian split that
# Fedora, Alpine and macOS do not have, so including it is a bell on three
# platforms to gain a handful of syntaxes on one. Specific completion syntax
# belongs in ~/.nanorc, which is yours and is not sent anywhere.
include "/usr/share/nano/*.nanorc"
